SUMMARY:Deadline: IJ4EU Freelancer Support Scheme 2026-27\, Second Call (cr
 oss-border teams of freelance journalists)
DESCRIPTION:A strand of IJ4EU for freelance journalists: teams of at least 
 two freelancers in two eligible countries receive funding\, training and m
 entoring for a cross-border investigation. TIMELINE: the second call opens
  1 December 2026 and closes 2 February 2027 (the scheme page shows it as p
 aused until then). No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Investigative Jour
 nalism for Europe (IJ4EU): International Press Institute and European Jour
 nalism Centre\nLocation: Remote. At least two freelancers based in two dif
 ferent eligible countries (EU27 plus several candidate and EEA countries\;
  the UK\, Moldova and Turkey count as third countries).\nAward: Up to EUR 
 20\,000 per team\, plus training and mentoring.\nDuration: Project-based c
 ross-border investigation.\n\nMore: https://investigativejournalismforeu.n
 et/grants/freelancer-support-scheme/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://investigativejournalismforeu.net/grants/freelancer-support-sche
 me/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote. At least two freelancers based in two different eligible c
 ountries (EU27 plus several candidate and EEA countries\; the UK\, Moldova
  and Turkey count as third countries).
END:VEVENT
